secureshellgo (1.7.0~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * AI Bridge: an assistant you paired can now ask to change a server
    (run a command, write a file, restart a service, open a terminal).
    Every change needs your yes on a card in the app, except commands you
    put on that server's "Allowed commands" list or a time-limited
    approval you gave. All of it is off by default, per server.
  * A terminal opened for an assistant is a session tab you can watch,
    take over or stop.
  * The activity log records how each change was allowed. The full list
    is in CHANGELOG.md.

