secureshellgo (1.6.0~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * AI Bridge, on Linux and Windows and off by default: an AI assistant on
    your computer can read from the servers you share, by name and
    read-only, without ever being given a password or key.
  * Settings has "Connect an assistant", "Paired assistants" (revoke any
    time), "Shared hosts" and an Activity list of every call made; "Connect
    Claude Code" sets it up in one step where the claude program is found.
  * A secureshellgo-mcp launcher in every package; one-click connect is not
    available in the snap or the Flatpak.
  * A backup keeps "Copy on select" and the app's language.
    The full list is in CHANGELOG.md.

